      "title": "POSITIVE - baby skin, no facial hair",
      "widgets_values": [
        "Photorealistic studio portrait photograph of an original 4-year-old East Asian girl, chest-up, facing the camera directly, looking into the lens. Straight black hair with blunt bangs cut just above the eyebrows, chin-length. Wearing a plain mint green cotton t-shirt. Mouth open in the middle of saying a short word, lips rounded on an 'o' sound.\n\nSKIN - CRITICAL: this is a young preschool child, so the skin must be perfectly smooth, plump, soft and luminous like a baby's. Absence of facial hair is mandatory: NO peach fuzz, NO vellus hair, NO beard shadow, NO stubble, NO dark hair strokes on the cheeks, NO hair on the upper lip, NO fuzz along the jaw or chin. The cheeks are clean, round, plump and smooth with a soft natural rosy blush. Poreless, flawlessly clean baby skin with a gentle natural sheen on the nose and forehead, subtle subsurface scattering making the skin look translucent and alive. Soft baby fat on the cheeks, a small rounded chin, delicate smooth neck.\n\nHair on the HEAD is rendered strand by strand with a few flyaway hairs catching the light, but the FACE itself is completely hair-free.\n\nLighting: large softbox 45 degrees camera-left, white reflector filling the right side, about 1.5:1 ratio, catchlights visible in both eyes, warm 3500K, even flattering falloff, no harsh shadows on the skin. Background: plain flat pale peach seamless studio backdrop, no gradient, no props, no floor line. Shot on an 85mm lens at f/2.0, shallow depth of field, sharp focus on the eyes, fine film grain at ISO 400. Square composition. No text, no logo, no watermark."
